<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Whig Party (United States)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1833">1833</a>–<a href="/years/1856">1856</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Whig Party was a political party of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> formed in the early 1830s by opponents of President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson">Andrew Jackson</a>. Led by figures such as Henry Clay and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daniel-webster">Daniel Webster</a>, it favoured a national bank, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protective-tariff">protective tariffs</a> and federal funding of roads and canals, won the presidency in 1840 and 1848, and broke apart over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in the 1850s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/whig-party-united-states.jpg" alt="Whig Party (United States)" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Terrence J. Kennedy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Whig_political_banner_by_Terrence_J._Kennedy.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Party politics emerged early, with Federalists against Jeffersonian Republicans, later Democrats against <b>Whigs</b> and, from the 1850s, Democrats against the new Republican Party.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-states">United States · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
